    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d50-a1">

                <pb facs="0170" n="112" xml:id="pg112"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 1.</seg></opener>
                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tlacotalpam</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 26, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Much Esteemed Friend:</hi> I have received your very
                    welcome duplicate letter of the 12th of December last, containing one from
                    President Juarez and documents, to be published here in relation to our
                    affairs.</p>
                <p>Our situation is about the same as it was when I, wrote you last; we still suffer
                    for want of arms and war materials. I enclose you the printed manifests of my
                    towns, approving of Señor Juarez’s continuance in power as President.</p>
                <p>Your devoted friend,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALEJANDRO GARCIA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Señor Don <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matias Romero</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
